              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hilaritās, hilaritātis — \"cheerfulness, merriment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hilaritās avī omnēs hospitēs laetōs facit. Grandfather's cheerfulness makes all the guests happy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, third declension. English hilarity comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hilaritās is built on hilaris \"cheerful\", an early borrowing from Greek hilaros \"cheerful\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English hilarity comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
